# Lovelace Project

Lovelace is a compiler (written in Ada) for a new Pascal/Ada/Delphi-like language. It emits WebAssembly **components** (`.wasm`) or WAT plus companion WIT. A host embedder can JIT-run those components via the Wasmtime C API.

## Products and link kinds

**`lovelace/lovelace/`** is the only host **executable** (crate `lovelace`). Every other host crate it uses is a **static** library (`Library_Kind use "static"` in the `.gpr`). Do **not** build `lovelace_compiler`, `lovelace_lir`, `lovelace_common`, `lovelace_jit`, `lovelace_tooling`, `lovelace_hypatia`, `lovelace_alexandria`, or `lovelace_format` as shared/dynamic libraries. Folder names stay as below; crate names start with `lovelace` (see utf8-and-naming).

The **only dynamic library** in the whole project is Augusta’s native backing (`.so` / `.dll` / `.dylib`) under `augusta/libaugusta/` (crate `lovelace_augusta` when created).

1. **`lovelace/compiler/`** — crate `lovelace_compiler`; static library: compiler (frontend, analysis, codegen).
2. **`jit/`** — crate `lovelace_jit`; static library: JIT runtime; **only** crate that links Wasmtime C (planned).
3. **`lovelace/lovelace/`** — crate `lovelace`; CLI executable (`lovelace compile`, `run`, `doc`, `format`, project/solution/package commands); statically links the host libraries.
4. **`augusta/`** — standard library: `.love` under `augusta/lovelace/`, native Ada under `augusta/libaugusta/`, web glue under `augusta/libaugusta-js/`. Flavors `native` / `wasi` / `web`.
5. **`lovelace/tooling/`** — crate `lovelace_tooling`; static library: `.pjlove`, `.slnlove`, `.pkglove` files and their behavior (planned).
6. **`hypatia/`** — crate `lovelace_hypatia`; static library: **Hypatia** package system (planned).
7. **`alexandria/`** — crate `lovelace_alexandria`; static library: parse Lovelace comments/doc-comments and generate documentation (planned).
8. **`format/`** — crate `lovelace_format`; static library: reformat `.love` to the effective style (planned).

Shared Ada under **`lovelace/`**: **`common/`** (`lovelace_common`), **`lir/`** (`lovelace_lir`) — both static libraries. Crate `lovelace_lir` owns LIR in-memory types and the versioned `.lir` / `.tlir` formats (not only analysis).

## Repository layout

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `scripts/` | Compile and run samples |
| `docs/` | Human documentation (CLI, grammar, HOW TOs, feature docs) |
| `lovelace/compiler/` | Compiler static library |
| `lovelace/common/` | Shared host static library |
| `lovelace/lir/` | LIR static library (types, `.lir` / `.tlir`) |
| `lovelace/lovelace/` | CLI executable |
| `lovelace/shared/` | Host GPR switch include + test helpers (not a crate) |
| `jit/` | JIT static library (Wasmtime; planned) |
| `lovelace/tooling/` | Project / solution / package static library (planned) |
| `hypatia/` | Hypatia package manager (static; planned) |
| `alexandria/` | Doc generation static library (planned) |
| `format/` | Source formatter static library (planned) |
| `augusta/lovelace/` | Augusta `.love` modules (in-tree `AUGUSTA_HOME`) |
| `augusta/libaugusta/` | Freestanding Ada native Augusta (**the only dynamic** library; planned) |
| `augusta/libaugusta-js/` | Web JS glue (planned) |
| `ide/lsp/` | Language Server Protocol for Lovelace and LIR (planned) |
| `ide/textmate/` | Shared TextMate grammars for `.love` and `.tlir` (planned; keep in sync with every language/TLIR surface change — see documentation rule) |
| `ide/vscode/` | VS Code extension (LSP + TextMate + build/run/debug; planned) |
| `ide/jetbrains/` | JetBrains plugin (WebStorm primary; planned) |
| `samples/` | `.love` samples under **feature subfolders** only (`samples/<feature>/…`; see samples rule) |

Build system is **Alire**: **one crate per Ada component**, plus a thin root crate `lovelace_workspace` that only `depends-on` + pins existing crates. See the Alire crates rule. Do not add further top-level **component** crates. Do not put several component GPRs in one `alire.toml`.

## Implement only what is asked

Build piece by piece when instructed. Do not scaffold the whole compiler, invent language syntax, or add crates/files beyond the current task. Create Alire crates only when that component is needed or the user asks.